/ A settings row saved before this stage still reads (ruling 7, decision 774). A saved
/ row is read into its class by its key (`<actor>!<path>`), which already says which
/ class — the row's own `kind` field is no longer the class picker. A row saved in
/ today's shape ({setting, kind: <path>}) reads back after the change. Guard — green
/ today (today's binary saves and reads today's shape); must stay green after. Settings
/ run in-memory under `--test` (setting-<app.id>, per PLang/app/actor/setting/this.cs),
/ so save+read in one run proves the round-trip; a committed sqlite fixture couldn't be
/ loaded in test mode (`Mode.Test` forces in-memory). The cross-binary read is proved by
/ the suite surviving the stage 2 change, not by this test alone.
OldSettingRowStillReads
- set %!llm.setting.cache% = "skip"
- save %!llm.setting%
- assert.equals(Expected="skip", Actual=%!llm.setting.cache%, Message="the saved cache value reads back")
- remove %!llm.setting%
